 bim:{sh:'bim',t:'Five-Story Office Building in a BIM Model',pre:'D3 Civil Engineering final project, 2026',a:'#2f6fd6',b:'#0d1b3a',
  m:[['Project','Office Building, 5 floors + rooftop'],['Campus','Politeknik Raflesia Rejang Lebong'],['Modeled in','Revit (Building Information Modeling)'],['Structural analysis','Robot Structural Analysis'],['Disciplines','Architecture, Structure, MEP']],
  d:'My final project: planning and modeling a five-story office building in Building Information Modeling with Autodesk Revit, then integrating the model with structural analysis in Robot Structural Analysis. One model produced 77 working drawing sheets: 32 architectural sheets, 24 structural sheets, and 21 MEP sheets (electrical, clean and waste water, HVAC). This experience sparked my interest in design coordination, working drawing development, and the use of BIM in construction projects. Click any sheet to view it in full.',
  f:[['77','Working drawing sheets'],['5 + Roof','Floors and rooftop, roof at +21.50 m'],['29 × 17.5 m','Floor plan, 9 × 7 axis grid'],['Ø60 · 14 m','Bored pile per point'],['400 × 400','Columns (mm), main beams 400 × 300']]},
 jembatan:{sh:'jbt',t:'Sample Bridge in a Revit Model',pre:'Revit modeling practice project',a:'#17a2b8',b:'#082b33',
  m:[['Type','Practice (dummy) project, not a field project'],['Modeled in','Revit'],['Drawing scope','Analytical plan, structural plan, bridge deck, 3D view, and elevations'],['Category','Bridge']],
  d:"Practice (dummy) project: a two-span concrete bridge model I built in Autodesk Revit to practice bridge structure modeling and drawing sheet preparation. This is not a field project. The model is 100 m long in total (2 × 50 m), consisting of abutments at both ends and a pier at mid-span resting on a pile cap and Ø450 mm concrete piles 24 m long, five girders per span, a 200 mm thick bridge deck, and concrete railings.\nFive sheets were produced from this model: analytical plan, structural plan, bridge deck, 3D view, and the east, west, north, and south elevations. Reference elevations on the views: railing +1.45 m, bridge deck ±0, girder bottom −2.00 m, and pile cap bottom −7.10 m. Click any sheet to view it in full.",
  f:[['2 × 50 m','Spans, 50 m girders'],['10.2 m','Bridge deck width'],['200 mm','Bridge deck thickness'],['Ø450 · 24 m','Concrete piles'],['5','Drawing sheets']]},
