  m:[['Category','Road'],['Work','Road geometric design and drive simulation'],['Scope','Existing ground surface, alignment, profile, superelevation, and corridor'],['Software','Autodesk Civil 3D']],
  d:'Road design modeling in Autodesk Civil 3D. The work starts from the existing ground surface (TIN surface) with contours, then defines the road alignment and builds the profile, including superelevation settings.\nFrom the alignment and profile, a road corridor is generated, and the result is reviewed through a drive simulation along the corridor to check the road shape and the slopes on both sides.',
